  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Living Heritage and The Sustainable Development Goals: Safeguarding intangible cultural heritage through formal and non-formal education in Asia and the Pacific and in Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project developed and piloted learning tools/pedagogies on the integration of living heritage in non-formal education in the Community Learning Centers in Nepal and Thailand aiming to strengthen the safeguarding and transmission of ICH, improve the relevance of education programmes and promote community well-being social cohesion and SD. Currently the project is being implemented in Benin, where it proposes to bring schools closer to communities and their social and cultural environment, to enhance the generational transmission of living heritage and to improve the academic performance of learners. The pilot phase will help evaluate and consolidate this method and approach before applying it to other regions.</narrative>
  </description>
